        "format_version": "0.5.10",
        "type": "model",
        "name": "NAFNet-GAN Noisy Nuclei Microscopy Denoiser",
        "description": "NAFNet-GAN is a supervised denoising model for 2D fluorescence microscopy images of nuclei acquired with widefield and confocal microscopy. It was developed for Dataset 3 of the AI4Life Microscopy Supervised Denoising Challenge 2025 and presented at ISBI 2026 in the paper “NAFNet-GAN: An Adversarial Framework for Supervised Fluorescence Microscopy Denoising.” The model was trained using both small and large nuclei-image crops to reduce severe acquisition noise while preserving nuclear structures and restoring the original input intensity range.",
        "authors": [
            {
                "name": "Guillermo Rey-Paniagua",
                "affiliation": "Universidad Carlos III de Madrid, Getafe, Madrid, Spain",
                "orcid": "0009-0001-1903-2892"
